A consumer demands a type alias to a pointer (type PN = *N). The value/pointer
bridge must recognize the alias as the pointer form and take the address (&n),
not dereference: bridgeDir unaliases the wanted type just as DualType/pointerElem
do when they pair the value and pointer duals.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
output: plumb_gen.go
-- example.com/app/app.go --
package app

type N struct{}

type PN = *N

//plumb:build
func MakeN() N { return N{} }

//plumb:build
func UseN(p PN) string { return "" }
